-- title:
--   Extending an admissible valuation to FullC level M'
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q\ge 5$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number not divisible by $q$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q$ a nonunit of $A$. Let $R_0$ be a constant reduction datum of $A$ from the base change $\overline{\mathcal F}=$ `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` (the Laurent-series base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of `modularFunctionFieldFull M'`, the subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\mathbb Q$ generated by the divisor expansions of level $M'$) to `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'`: that is, a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ of $\overline{\mathcal F}$ whose intersection with $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is $A$, a surjective residue map onto `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` with kernel the maximal ideal and compatible with reduction on $A$, together with a degree-preserving map on places satisfying the order-compatibility of the structure, and such that every $f$ in $\overline{\mathcal F}$ has a nonzero residue after scaling by a constant. Assume $R_0$ is compatible with coefficientwise reduction: for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose image in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $\overline{\mathcal F}$, that image lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its residue, read as a Laurent series over the residue field of $A$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$. Let $\mathcal A$ be a subring of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\mathbb Q$ consisting exactly of those $gf$ lying in `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose base change lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and which satisfy $\operatorname{ord}_P(gf)\ge 0$ at every place $P$ of $\overline{\mathcal F}$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\operatorname{ord}_P(jq)\ge 0$; assume $jq\in\mathcal A$. Let $\Omega$ be a field which is an algebra over the residue field $\kappa$ of $A$, and let $\mathrm{val}:\mathcal A\to\Omega$ be a ring homomorphism which vanishes at every element of $\mathcal A$ whose $R_0$-residue is $0$, and for which $\mathrm{val}(jq)$ is transcendental over $\kappa$. Then there is a $\kappa$-algebra homomorphism $\mathrm{emb}$ from `modularFunctionFieldFullC κ M'` (the subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\kappa$ generated by the characteristic-$q$ divisor expansions of level $M'$) to $\Omega$ such that for every $gf\in\mathcal A$ the image under $\mathrm{emb}$ of the $R_0$-residue of $gf$, included into `modularFunctionFieldFullC κ M'`, equals $\mathrm{val}(gf)$.
--
--   This is the extension step for readings of the reduced full-level modular function field: a ring-valued specialisation defined only on the admissible rational functions regular where $j$ is regular, and killing those with zero residue, is shown to come from a $\kappa$-algebra embedding of the whole characteristic-$q$ full level-$M'$ function field. It is used in the construction of such embeddings from Tate points, the statement [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_algHom_modularFunctionFieldFullC_forall_apply_residue_eq_ringHom_of_transcendental_of_tatePoint`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_algHom_modularFunctionFieldFullC_forall_apply_residue_eq_ringHom_of_transcendental_of_tatePoint).
